 separate mention from the long form.\",\"guideline_section\":\"6. Annotate all synonymous mentions\"},{\"start\":216,\"end\":244,\"text\":\"autosomal recessive disorder\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Refers to a genetically inherited family of diseases, matching the guideline example of autosomal recessive disease as a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class); Examples item 10\"},{\"start\":306,\"end\":319,\"text\":\"periodontitis\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rationale\":\"Named disease with a single definition describing severe periodontal inflammation.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Specific Disease)\"},{\"start\":440,\"end\":462,\"text\":\"Palmoplantar keratosis\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Duplicate mention of palmoplantar keratosis, a family of varying skin conditions, in a new sentence.\",\"guideline_section\":\"4. Annotate duplicate mentions; 1. Disease Class\"},{\"start\":516,\"end\":530,\"text\":\"hyperkeratosis\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Refers to a group of skin thickening conditions, so it is treated as a Disease Class mention rather than a general term.\",\"guideline_section\":\"1. Annotate all Specific Disease mentions (Disease Class)\"},{\"start\":591,\"end\":600,\"text\":\"Keratosis\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Refers to the same keratosis condition affecting other body sites, a family of skin conditions. Annotated as a duplicate mention of the disease class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"4. Annotate duplicate mentions; 1. Disease Class\"},{\"start\":658,\"end\":661,\"text\":\"PLS\",\"entity\":\"Modifier\",\"rationale\":\"Disease abbreviation used as a modifier of the noun 'patients', so it is annotated as a Modifier.\",\"guideline_section\":\"3. Annotate disease mentions used as Modifiers\"},{\"start\":684,\"end\":697,\"text\":\"periodontitis\",\"entity\":\"SpecificDisease\",\"rational